---
title: Chicken noodle soup
servings: 4
yield: 4 to 6 servings
tags: [american, chicken, one-pot, weeknight]
cuisine: american
time: 1 hour
source: Easy Chicken Noodle Soup by Jennifer Segal, Once Upon a Chef, https://www.onceuponachef.com/recipes/chicken-noodle-soup.html
---

Season the @chicken thighs{2%lb}(bone-in, skin-on; or breasts) with
@salt{3/4%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}.

Heat the @vegetable oil{1%tbsp} in a #Dutch oven{} over medium-high heat. Brown
the chicken skin side down ~{5%minutes}, then turn and cook ~{4%minutes} more.

Add the @chicken broth{8%cup}, @yellow onion{1}(chopped),
@carrots{2}(in 1/2-inch pieces), @celery{2%ribs}(in 1/4-inch pieces),
@fresh thyme{4%sprigs} and @bay leaf{1}. Scrape up the browned bits.

Bring to a boil, cover, and simmer on low until the chicken is cooked,
~{20%minutes} for thighs or about 15 for breasts.

Fish out the thyme and bay leaf. Lift the chicken onto a board and shred it,
throwing away the skin and bones.

Bring the soup back to a boil and cook the @egg noodles{5%oz}(wide) in it,
uncovered, until al dente.

Return the chicken and heat through over medium heat for a few minutes. Season
to taste and stir in the @fresh dill{2%tbsp}(minced).

> To keep it, store the chicken and noodles apart from the broth; the noodles
> drink the soup overnight.
